\61\74\65\64\20\74\68\6F\75\67\68\2E\00Mixer sample rate, setting any device's rate higher than this will probably lower their sound quality.\001024\002048\004096\008192\00512\00256\00Mixer block size, larger blocks might help sound stuttering but sound will also be more lagged.\00How many milliseconds of data to keep on top of the blocksize.\00midi\00win32\00alsa\00coreaudio\00coremidi\00Type of MPU-401 to emulate.\00Device that will receive the MIDI data from MPU-401.\00Special configuration options for the device driver. This is usually the id of the device you want to use.
  or in the case of coreaudio, you can specify a soundfont here.
  When using a Roland MT-32 rev. 0 as midi output device, some games may require a delay in order to prevent 'buffer overflow' issues.
  In that case, add 'delaysysex', for example: midiconfig=2 delaysysex
  See the README/Manual for more details.\00sblaster\00Type of Soundblaster to emulate. gb is Gameblaster.\00The IO address of the soundblaster.\00The IRQ number of the soundblaster.\00The DMA number of the soundblaster.\00The High DMA number of the soundblaster.\00Allow the soundblaster mixer to modify the DOSBox mixer.\00Type of OPL emulation. On 'auto' the mode is determined by sblaster type. All OPL modes are Adlib-compatible, except for 'cms'.\00Provider for the OPL emulation. compat might provide better quality (see oplrate as well).\00Sample rate of OPL music emulation. Use 49716 for highest quality (set the mixer rate accordingly).\00Enable the Gravis Ultrasound emulation.\00Sample rate of Ultrasound emulation.\00The IO base address of the Gravis Ultrasound.\00The IRQ number of the Gravis Ultrasound.\00The DMA channel of the Gravis Ultrasound.\00C:\ULTRASND\00Path to Ultrasound directory. In this directory
there should be a MIDI directory that contains
the patch files for GUS playback. Patch sets used
with Timidity should work fine.\00speaker\00Enable PC-Speaker emulation.\00Sample rate of the PC-Speaker sound generation.\00Enable Tandy Sound System emulation. For 'auto', emulation is present only if machine is set to 'tandy'.\00Sample rate of the Tandy 3-Voice generation.\00Enable Disney Sound Source emulation. (Covox Voice Master and Speech Thing compatible).\00joystick\00Type of joystick to emulate: auto (default), none,
2axis (supports two joysticks),
4axis (supports one joystick, first joystick used),
4axis_2 (supports one joystick, second joystick used),
fcs (Thrustmaster), ch (CH Flightstick).
none disables joystick emulation.
auto chooses emulation depending on real joystick(s).
(Remember to reset dosbox's mapperfile if you saved it earlier)\00enable timed intervals for axis. Experiment with this option, if your joystick drifts (away).\00continuously fires as long as you keep the button pressed.\00swap the 3rd and the 4th axis. can be useful for certain joysticks.\00enable button wrapping at the number of emulated buttons.\00serial\00modem\00nullmodem\00directserial\00serial1\00set type of device connected to com port.
Can be disabled, dummy, modem, nullmodem, directserial.
Additional parameters must be in the same line in the form of
parameter:value. Parameter for all types is irq (optional).
for directserial: realport (required), rxdelay (optional).
                 (realport:COM1 realport:ttyS0).
for modem: listenport (optional).
for nullmodem: server, rxdelay, txdelay, telnet, usedtr,
               transparent, port, inhsocket (all optional).
Example: serial1=modem listenport:5000\00serial2\00see serial1\00serial3\00serial4\00Enable XMS support.\00Enable EMS support. The default (=true) provides the best
compatibility but certain applications may run better with
other choices, or require EMS support to be disabled (=false)
to work at all.\00Enable UMB support.\00Language code of the keyboard layout (or none).\00Lines in this section will be run at startup.
You can put your MOUNT lines here.
